# Front-End Stack Rules
- Framework: Next.js 14+ (App Router, Strict TypeScript)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS, Dark Mode default, Shadcn/ui conventions
- Structure: Follow atomic design pattern in apps/web/src/components

# 3D Engineering Rules
- Library: PlayCanvas Engine (Latest stable release)
- Environment Separation: NEVER import React/Next state hooks into packages/core-3d. Keep the 3D pipeline completely headless, controlled purely through native DOM events or a crisp pub/sub event emitter class.
- Performance Rule: All math, vector operations, and matrix transformations must run inside packages/core-3d to maximize frames-per-second (FPS).

# AI Coding Style
- Write production-grade, typed, modular code ready for senior developer handoff.
- Avoid loose or 'any' type assertions in TypeScript. Use descriptive comments on heavy mathematical functions.
- If rewriting an existing file, keep existing functional code intact unless explicitly asked to refactor.
